House Speaker Mike Johnson warned that a moratorium could weaken American technological

00:05:25.606 --> 00:05:31.486
competitiveness while President Trump has opposed restrictions on similar grounds. Resolution

00:05:31.486 --> 00:05:36.786
depends on whether Congress or state regulators imposed binding limits before the next construction

00:05:36.786 --> 00:05:42.910
cycle. Hidden inside that vendor pick is the engineering angle. How many bits you can push through

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:49.650
a tower before the utility drop says stop. A massive MIMO panel is a phased array, so each extra

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:55.410
transmit path lets you add the same radio wave in phase toward one user and cancel it toward another,

00:05:55.790 --> 00:06:00.210
and one frequency channel can be reused across people standing in different directions.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:07.730
distance. Earlier macros often ran 8 transmit and 8 receive paths, then 32 and 32. Denser

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:12.590
arrays form narrower, higher gain beams without asking the regulator for more megahertz.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:18.310
For a midband carrier near 2 gigahertz, the wavelength is about 15 centimeters and half

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:24.190
wavelength spacing sits around 7.5 centimeters, so a few dozen element panels still fits on

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:29.350
a face a couple of meters on a side. A back of envelope array gain is 10 times the base

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:35.270
10 log of the element count. About 18 decibels at this scale versus about 9 on an 8-path

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:41.090
radio. Roughly 8 times the power density in the wanted beam. Integrating radio frequency

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:46.170
processing and latency-sensitive physical layer functions into one compact set of boxes

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:51.470
cuts the discrete enclosures that each need power and cooling, which is the kilowatt-hour

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:57.210
lever across a national footprint. If that saves even 500 watts at a site, a rough estimate,

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:02.490
not a vendor spec, it is often the difference between the existing utility drop and a new grid

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:08.270
interconnection. The idiot index on a weatherproof radio can sit around 10, meaning the finished

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:14.050
unit costs on the order of 10 times the silicon, copper, and aluminum inside it, because filters,

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:19.870
calibration, and certification dominate. The magic wand number is kilowatt hours at the tower.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:25.290
Even if electricity were free, heat and the local drop would still cap the radios you can hang.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:33.290
low-band wavelengths stretched to a meter or more, punch through walls and let you build fewer macros while mid-band carries capacity.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:41.590
Satellite backhaul can reach towers that would otherwise wait on fiber. Light time from low-earth orbit is on the order of a couple of milliseconds,

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:47.010
so a consistent orbital to ground handoff is a protocol problem more than a physics problem.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:53.650
A radar engineer would recognize the same trick. You do not make the transmitter stronger, you make the beam narrower,

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:57.830
so the watt that used to heat the horizon now lands on one hand set.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.350
Spatial degrees of freedom got cheaper than buying new spectrum.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.210
That is also why backhaul at the site matters.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:09.710
A tower that cannot get fiber can still take a radio if the power drop and the link both exist.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:13.130
And the power drop is the one that permitting actually counts.

